Q. Storage gateway (hybrid solution)?
A:	AWS Storage Gateway – A hybrid cloud storage service that connects your on-premises environment to AWS storage.
It lets you store data locally for quick access while backing it up or extending it to AWS.
Type
Purpose
Example Use
File Gateway
Store/retrieve files via NFS/SMB; backed by S3
File shares, backups
Volume Gateway
Cloud-backed iSCSI volumes (stored or cached)
App storage, disaster recovery
Tape Gateway
Virtual tape library in AWS
Replacing physical tape backups


Q. S3 Bucket lifecycle?
A:	S3 Bucket Lifecycle – Rules that automatically manage object storage over time to save cost and optimize storage.
Main Actions in Lifecycle Rules:
Transition → Move objects to cheaper storage classes (e.g., S3 Standard → S3 Glacier).
Expiration → Delete objects after a certain time.
Noncurrent Version Expiration → Delete older versions if versioning is enabled.

